<title>GERMANY: Daimler, Ford hold off Germany sick pay cuts.</title>
<headline>Daimler, Ford hold off Germany sick pay cuts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German auto giant Daimler-Benz AG said on Monday it would suspend sick pay cuts it had announced earlier while talks go on between metal industry employers and union leaders on resolving a row over the issue.</p>
<p>A spokesman at Daimler headquarters in Stuttgart said the group's 220,000 employees would receive full sick pay while the talks continue. The Gesamtmetall employers' group and the IG Metall union will meet again on October 10 after talks on Monday.</p>
<p>Ford-Werke AG, the German unit of U.S. Ford Motor Co, also said in a statement that it would continue to pay full sick pay until December 31, in accordance with pay contracts.</p>
</text>
